<title>RUSSIA: Russian Sept inflation 0.3 pct vs 0.2 pct fall.</title>
<headline>Russian Sept inflation 0.3 pct vs 0.2 pct fall.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's monthly consumer price inflation was 0.3 percent in September after a price decline of 0.2 percent in August, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN CONSUMER PRICES    SEP 96    AUG 96    SEP 95</p>
<p>    Month-on-month change	 +0.3	-0.2	+4.6</p>
<p>    Year-on-year change	    n/a     +37.1    +225</p>
<p>				    w/e Sept 30	   w/e Sept 23</p>
<p>    Week-on-week change	   +0.1		    +0.1</p>
<p>					 Sept 1-30	     Aug 1-31</p>
<p>    Average daily inflation     +0.011		  -0.007</p>
<p>The committee said consumer prices had risen 16.5 percent so far this year. If current price trends continue, the year-on-year price rise in December will be 17.7 percent, it said.</p>
<p>--Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
